ties</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Net cash provided by operating activities in 2025 was RMB119.1 million (US$17.0 million) and primarily consisted of our net loss of RMB22.5 million (US$3.2 million), as adjusted for non-cash items and the effects of changes in operating assets and liabilities. Adjustment for non-cash items primarily included RMB10.0 million (US$1.4 million) of share-based compensation, RMB1.8 million (US$0.3 million) of inventory write-down and RMB38.7 million (US$5.5 million) of noncash lease expense. In 2025, the principal items accounting for the changes in operating assets and liabilities were increase in accounts payable of RMB439.1 million (US$62.8 million) and a decrease in accounts receivable of RMB150.5 million (US$21.5 million). The decrease in accounts receivable was primarily due to the decline in revenue resulting from our strategic transition towards an asset-light business model.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Net cash provided by operating activities in 2024 was RMB263.0 million and primarily consisted of our net loss of RMB20.8 million, as adjusted for non-cash items and the effects of changes in operating assets and liabilities. Adjustment for non-cash items primarily included RMB20.1 million of share-based compensation, RMB3.9 million of inventory write-down and RMB48.5 million of noncash lease expense. In 2024, the principal items accounting for the changes in operating assets and liabilities were increase in accounts payable of RMB132.7 million and a decrease in accounts receivable of RMB123.2 million. The decrease in accounts receivable was primarily due to a decrease in revenue and the increase in accounts payable was primarily due to the expanded use of bank bill settlement.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Net cash used in operating activities in 2023 was RMB447.2 million and primarily consisted of our net loss of RMB353.4 million, as adjusted for non-cash items and the effects of changes in operating assets and liabilities. Adjustment for non-cash items primarily included RMB226.7 million of share-based compensation, RMB19.9 million of inventory write-down and RMB62.6 million of noncash lease expense, partially offset by an increase in investment income of RMB4.0 million. In 2023, the principal items accounting for the changes in operating assets and liabilities were decrease in accounts payable of RMB176.7 million and a decrease in accrued expense and other current liabilities of RMB229.9 million. The decrease in accrued expense and other current liabilities account was primarily due to the decrease in advance from customers.</p><p style="color:#404040;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 7.2pt;"><span style="color:#000000;">Investing Activities</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Net cash used in investing activities in 2025 was RMB53.7 million (US$7.7 million), consisting primarily of purchases of short-term investments of RMB750.0 million (US$107.2 million), partially offset by proceeds from sale or maturity of short-term investments of RMB700.6 million (US$100.2 million).</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Net cash provided by investing activities in 2024 was RMB37.4 million, consisting primarily of purchases of short-term investments of RMB460.0 million, partially offset by proceeds from sale or maturity of short-term investments of RMB511.2 million.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Net cash provided by investing activities in 2023 was RMB151.7 million, consisting primarily of purchases of short-term investments of RMB914.3 million, partially offset by proceeds from sale or maturity of short-term investments of RMB1,074.2 million.</p></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">105</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><p style="color:#404040;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 7.2pt;"><span style="color:#000000;">Financing Activities</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Net cash used in financing activities in 2025 was RMB21.2 million (US$3.0 million), consisting of proceeds from short-term bank borrowings of RMB287.6 million (US$41.1 million) partially offset by repayment of short-term bank borrowings of RMB261.0 million (US$37.3 million) and proceeds from other financing arrangement of RMB53.5 million (US$7.6 million) partially offset by repayment under other financing arrangement of RMB97.0 million (US$13.9 million) and repayment of redemption rights from redeemable non-controlling interest holders of RMB3.2 million (US$0.5 million), and payment for share repurchase from non-controlling interest holders of RMB1.9 million (US$0.3 million).</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Net cash used in financing activities in 2024 was RMB406.2 million, consisting of proceeds from short-term bank borrowings of RMB438.9 million partially offset by repayment of short-term bank borrowings of RMB616.0 million and proceeds from other financing arrangement of RMB711.0 million partially offset by repayment under other financing arrangement of RMB840.3 million and repayment of redemption rights from redeemable non-controlling interest holders of RMB87.5 million, and payment for share repurchase from non-controlling interest holders of RMB13.5 million.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Net cash provided by financing activities in 2023 was RMB206.0 million, consisting of proceeds from short-term bank borrowings of RMB919.6 million, partially offset by repayment of short-term bank borrowings of RMB750.1 million and proceeds from other financing arrangement of RMB1,451.4 million, partially offset by repayment under other financing arrangement of RMB1,415.1 million.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Material Cash Requirements</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Our material cash requirements as of December 31, 2025 and any subsequent interim period primarily include our capital expenditures and operating lease commitments. As of December 31, 2025, we have a total outstanding amount of RMB1.1 billion, which has been included in the balances of redeemable non-controlling interests and accrued expenses and other current liabilities, owed to a group of investors of 1 Pharmacy Technology pursuant to their equity investments made in 2020. See &#8220;Item 4. Information on the Company &#8212; A. History and Development of the Company.&#8221; 111 received redemption requests from certain of such investors in accordance with the terms of their initial investments in 1 Pharmacy Technology. Other than those as discussed below, we did not have any significant capital and other commitments, long-term obligations or guarantees as of December 31, 2025. We did not have future minimum capital commitments as of December 31, 2023, 2024, and 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 7.2pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Capital Expenditures</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">We made capital expenditures of RMB9.8 million, RMB15.2 million and RMB4.5 million (US$0.6 million) in 2023, 2024, and 2025, respectively. In these periods, our capital expenditures were primarily used for purchases of property, equipment and software to establish more fulfillment centers to meet the expected growth of our business.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 7.2pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Operating lease commitments</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The following table sets forth our operating lease commitments as of December 31, 2025:</p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:100%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:49.45%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:12pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.02%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt