ground:#cceeff;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> &#8212;</p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:75.83%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;">The outstanding confirmed amount at the end of the year</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.5%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;">&#160;</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:9.58%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> &#8212;</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.5%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;">&#160;</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:9.58%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_eLIlXpzezkeI9ErqwFtpng" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_us-gaap_CollaborativeArrangementTransactionWithPartyToCollaborativeArrangementAndThirdPartyMember_o-TDSQGXckeUFEe8sjOJeg" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yi:LiabilityUnderReverseFactoringProgramCurrent" scale="3" id="Tc_kIPpGAKRV0C2452rmMjPgw_6_4">19,800</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr></table></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;padding-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><i style="font-style:italic;">Factoring program</i></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In 2021, the Group entered into factoring agreement with recourse with a third-party financial institution, pursuant to which the institution will make an advance payment of accounts with credit term of 30 days typically. The term of the loan is mostly three months. The agreement requires that the entity provide RMB <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_eLIlXpzezkeI9ErqwFtpng" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2021_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_us-gaap_CollaborativeArrangementTransactionWithPartyToCollaborativeArrangementAndThirdPartyMember_0VEcS1a7OEeI44MUAGDa7Q" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SecurityDepositLiability" scale="3" id="Narr_AhWBit-oOkucIWiVBTlxgg">2,000</ix:nonFraction> as security deposit for the factoring arrangement, the factoring agreement ended in July 2, 2024. The interest rate charged from the institution was at annual rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_uVtV7QW_90GfInde3yRR7A" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2021_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_us-gaap_CollaborativeArrangementTransactionWithPartyToCollaborativeArrangementAndThirdPartyMember_0VEcS1a7OEeI44MUAGDa7Q" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_o6OWrvjYyE60LcHgDLFalA">8.5</ix:nonFraction>% in 2021, renewed in 2022 of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_uVtV7QW_90GfInde3yRR7A" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2022_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_us-gaap_CollaborativeArrangementTransactionWithPartyToCollaborativeArrangementAndThirdPartyMember_nbvn1CR5hkqQQiZixuBz5A" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_B-eIBxNAtEOSfAzfc_gJDw">9</ix:nonFraction>%, renewed in 2023 of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_uVtV7QW_90GfInde3yRR7A" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2023_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_us-gaap_CollaborativeArrangementTransactionWithPartyToCollaborativeArrangementAndThirdPartyMember_s_fW9wBRNkm8mpxKHfYbXQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_BNOryPka_kmBfyIYHP6iKA">10.5</ix:nonFraction>% and remained the same through the expiry of the agreement. In 2024, the Group entered into a new factoring agreement with recourse with a third - party financial institution, pursuant to which it transferred all legally held accounts receivable under the underlying contracts to the institution. The term of the loan is mostly six months. The agreement does not require the Group to provide any security deposit. Under this factoring agreement, the principal amount of financing shall not exceed RMB <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_eLIlXpzezkeI9ErqwFtpng" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_us-gaap_CollaborativeArrangementTransactionWithPartyToCollaborativeArrangementAndThirdPartyMember_KpZMek1_m0G85tez_n1s6Q" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yi:LiabilityUnderFactoringProgramCurrent" scale="3" id="Narr_EJ230bRO0EKbItA-EF5-eA">30,000</ix:nonFraction>. The factoring fees charged from the institution were RMB <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_eLIlXpzezkeI9ErqwFtpng" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_1v8us4Jp0UWZ3sT2dFUDWQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yi:FactoringFeeExpense" scale="3" id="Narr_qzW9R2yb90qOhAoyu9cPmw">2,121</ix:nonFraction> for the year ended December 31, 2024. The agreement has expired on February 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Group does not derecognize accounts receivable when receiving advance payment from the institution. The Group is required to pay the principal and interest to the institution on due. The proceeds from the institution used to settle the accounts receivable and subsequent repayment to the financial institution are considered financing activities and reported as &#8220;Proceeds from other financing activities&#8221; and &#8220;Repayment for other financing activities&#8221; on the consolidated statements of cash flows, respectively.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of December 31, 2024 and 2025, the outstanding borrowings from the factoring arrangements were RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_eLIlXpzezkeI9ErqwFtpng" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_82E2ueFdN0CT3svpL9I0Pw" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yi:LiabilityUnderFactoringProgramCurrent" scale="3" id="Narr_uFjU1hNK00Sx2LXXGcm4BQ">30,000</ix:nonFraction> and RMB <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_eLIlXpzezkeI9ErqwFtpng" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_bDTWtOASv0OOLgYE-Kqt3A" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="yi:LiabilityUnderFactoringProgramCurrent" scale="3" id="Narr_RN-MjzUDXkehC9m2PSKOFA">nil</ix:nonFraction>, respectively, which is repayable within one year and are included in &#8220;Accrued expenses and other current liabilities&#8221; on the consolidated balance sheets. The rollforward of outstanding borrowing from the factoring arrangements for years ended December 31, 2024, and 2025, are as follows:</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:12pt;line-height:1.31;margin:0pt 0pt 6pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin-bottom:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:continuation></ix:continuation></div><div s