name="us-gaap:ShortTermBorrowings" scale="3" id="Narr_sGYkuFveN0-Fxlw-4YedDg">187,631</ix:nonFraction> as of December 31, 2024 and 2025, respectively, all of which consisted of borrowings from financial institutions and are repayable within one year. As of December 31, 2025, the Group had an undrawn balance of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_eLIlXpzezkeI9ErqwFtpng" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_eC8yuKUkCkawfuJbYXO4DA" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityRemainingBorrowingCapacity" scale="3" id="Narr_UlmzptZHwUqoIBdSiH_iyQ">112,369</ix:nonFraction> under the credit facilities agreement. All of these borrowings were unsecured and accrue interest at an average annual interest rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_uVtV7QW_90GfInde3yRR7A" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_ATDpO2emS0qlzCkxAarWBg" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityInterestRateAtPeriodEnd" scale="-2" id="Narr_Fni3Z1BEGk6rMWE2vu5LlA">3.67</ix:nonFraction>% and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_uVtV7QW_90GfInde3yRR7A" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_eC8yuKUkCkawfuJbYXO4DA" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityInterestRateAtPeriodEnd" scale="-2" id="Narr_Apaq48eqN0ODiEk5NoN5IA">2.69</ix:nonFraction>% for the years ended December 31, 2024 and 2025, respectively.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In September 2019, 1 Pharmacy Technology entered into a credit agreement with China Merchant Bank (CMB) which provides a revolving credit facility that allows 1 Pharmacy Technology to borrow up to RMB <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_X53jV-FGJEaGdXirjDcT1g" contextRef="As_Of_9_30_2019_dei_LegalEntityAxis_yi_OnePharmacyTechnologyShanghaiCoLtdMember_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_LineOfCreditFacilityAxis_yi_ChinaMerchantBankMember_jLccwHYebUqGS-Y2TSA8PA" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="3" id="Narr_MELRuCBghEu6owA6QLbBPg">100,000</ix:nonFraction> for working capital purpose in one year. In October 2020, November 2021, December 2022 and December 2023, 1 Pharmacy Technology renewed the credit agreement that allowed 1 Pharmacy Technology to borrow up to RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_eLIlXpzezkeI9ErqwFtpng" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_dei_LegalEntityAxis_yi_OnePharmacyTechnologyShanghaiCoLtdMember_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_LineOfCreditFacilityAxis_yi_ChinaMerchantBankMember_XpeqwKQqgUuZrnyqb0RC9w" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="3" id="Narr_aQ6V5CfFfECixPS9D_Vi1w">200,000</ix:nonFraction> for working capital purposes for another one year and expired on January 2025. Any draw down on the credit facility will be charged with interest at one-year loan prime rate published by People&#8217;s Bank of China plus <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_uVtV7QW_90GfInde3yRR7A" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2019_To_9_30_2019_dei_LegalEntityAxis_yi_OnePharmacyTechnologyShanghaiCoLtdMember_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_LineOfCreditFacilityAxis_yi_ChinaMerchantBankMember_ITiiiRAHj0qLdG5Pq_-ymQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_VfcpjO_bnkG89PCBj7_RcA">0.30</ix:nonFraction>%. The borrowings were guaranteed by Yihao Pharmacy. During the years ended December 31, 2024 and 2025, RMB <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_eLIlXpzezkeI9ErqwFtpng" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024